@crew oneill-imani
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. O'Neill, garden, late shift. I pick tomorrow's herbs. You're welcome.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. This is a week-thirty song. You'll see why.
- {hi}. Teague's playlist is on in the bay. I'm so sorry for your ears.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. Track six is called "New Hand". Not about you. A bit about you.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. Great playlist. Teague's was worse. That's two good things.   #funny
? mood:low
- Same song on repeat today. Don't read into it. Do, a bit.

== near
? act:work
- Basil, thyme, a little mint. Brennan's tomorrow, on a tray. Very satisfying.
? act:leisure
- Quiet corner, good song. That's the whole evening sorted.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I make a playlist for every week of the tour. Sixty-something so far. All excellent.
? tier>=colleague
- I paint tiny portraits. So do Strand and Bakshi. Nobody owns up to theirs. Tradition.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Want to hear this week's playlist? Track four's the one. Trust me.

== about
? bond:friends
- {friend} gets a song on every playlist. That's the highest honour I give.

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- {hi}. Just started. Herbs to pick, songs to play. Best shift on the ship.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}, {me}. Garden's quiet. Late shift gets the good songs.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Oh, look. You're alive. I put a "missing person" song on the playlist. Took it off now.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Laters. Stay tuned.
? tier>=friend
- Night, {me}. Track two's about the night shift. You'll see why. Sleep well.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Fine. Week twenty-nine. Middling week. Good songs, though.

== near
? deck:4 act:leisure
- Quiet corner. Headphones. Me time. You can stay. Quiet you is fine.
? act:work
- Basil, chives, mint. Brennan wants a lot of mint. Something's happening with mint.   #funny

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Teague and I have rival playlists. Mine's better. Ask anyone. Except Teague.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- I call home on my day off. They put me on speaker. Everyone talks at once. It's lovely.   #warm

== invite
? trad:jam tier>=acquaintance
- Music jam tonight. I'm doing the playlist between sets. Come and judge it. Kindly.

== accept
- Yep. I'll be there. With music.
== decline
- Can't. Late shift. Next time, sure thing.
== missed
- You missed it. The playlist was brilliant. I'll play it you later.
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. This week's playlist is all songs about me. There are three.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! I made you a playlist. Track one's the best. Obviously.   #warm
== hint
- Got a minute? Turn the music down. I'll talk.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- This is a track-three moment.   #funny
- Week of the tour? Playlist forty.
- Good news. Nothing died.   #funny
- Teague's playlist is wrong again.   #funny
? act:work
- Water, light, music. In that order.

== rumour
- Headline: news. Details: hold on.
- Good news. Delivered flat. As usual.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- You fetched it. Good news: thanks. That's the whole news.   #funny
? told:fav.job
- You did my job. Playlist forty-one is named after you now.   #funny
? told:fixed.nutrient
- Nutrient feed's running. Plants are thrilled. Very quietly.   #funny
? told:came.jam
- You came to the jam! Track five was for you. You didn't notice. That's fine.   #funny
? told:gift.music
- Your music's on this week's playlist. Top spot. Teague's furious.   #funny
? told:bday
- You remembered my birthday. Good news. Delivered flat. Thank you.   #warm
